A certificate was issued to log in as you at a console: a physical terminal, a
serial console, or a BMC viewer on the machine below.

If you just typed a code from that screen into the web UI and approved the
login, this is it.

If you did not, someone got a console login in your name approved, which takes
your web session. Sign out everywhere, change whatever protects your identity
provider account, then tell whoever runs that machine: the certificate is live
until it expires and cannot be recalled.

CERTIFICATE

A console certificate authorizes one login session on that machine. It is not
an SSH login credential and cannot open a session elsewhere.

